 \\times 9 = 18\\) (write 8, carry 1).\n   - Hundreds place: \\(3 \\times 9 + 1 = 28\\) (write 8, carry 2).\n   - Continue this pattern for all digits. Each multiplication results in a digit 8 with varying carries, except the final step:\n   - Hundred-millions place: \\(9 \\times 9 + 7 = 88\\) (write 8, carry 8).\n   - Billions place: The final carryover 8 is added as the highest digit.\n\n   The product is \\(8,888,888,889\\).\n\n2. **Verification via Subtraction**:  \n   Recognize \\(987654321 = 1,000,000,000 - 12,345,679\\). Thus:\n   \\[\n   987654321 \\times 9 = (1,000,000,000 - 12,345,679) \\times 9 = 9,000,000,000 - 111,111,111 = 8,888,888,889.\n   \\]\n\n3. **Digit Analysis**:  \n   The result \\(8,888,888,889\\) contains the digit **9** only once in the units place. All other digits are **8**.\n\n**Answer**: The digit 9 appears **1 time** in the product.  \n**Correct Option**: \\(\\boxed{B}\\)", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. Given the problem: How many times does the digit 9 appear in the answer to $987654321 \\times 9$?\n   \n2. We will start by performing the multiplication: \n\n   \\[\n   987654321 \\times 9\n   \\]\n   \n3. Perform the multiplication step-by-step:\n   - Multiply from right to left, digit by digit: \n   \n     \\[\n     \\begin{array}{r}\n       987654321 \\\\\n     \\times 9 \\\\\n     \\hline\n       8888888889 \\\\\n     \\end{array}\n     \\]\n   \n   Breaking it down:\n   - \\( 1 \\times 9 = 9 \\)\n   - \\( 2 \\times 9 = 18 \\) (write 8, carry 1)\n   - \\( 3 \\times 9 + 1 = 28 \\) (write 8, carry 2)\n   - \\( 4 \\times 9 + 2 = 38 \\) (write 8, carry 3)\n   - \\( 5 \\times 9 + 3 = 48 \\) (write 8, carry 4)\n   - \\( 6 \\times 9 + 4 = 58 \\) (write 8, carry 5)\n   - \\( 7 \\times 9 + 5 = 68 \\) (write 8, carry 6)\n   - \\( 8 \\times 9 + 6 = 78 \\) (write 8, carry 7)\n   - \\( 9 \\times 9 + 7 = 88 \\) (write 8, carry 8)\n   \n   Therefore, we get the answer as:\n\n   \\[\n   987654321 \\times 9 = 8888888889 \n   \\]\n\n4. Now, count t