t - b)(t - b) ) ] |.\n\nSimplify denominator of the big fraction:\n\n1 + (s k^2)/( (st - b)(t - b) ) = [ (st - b)(t - b) + s k^2 ] / (st - b)(t - b)\n\nTherefore, the entire expression becomes:\n\n1/t = | [ b(1 - s) / ( (st - b)(t - b) ) ] / [ ( (st - b)(t - b) + s k^2 ) / ( (st - b)(t - b) ) ) ] |.\n\nSimplify the division:\n\n= | [ b(1 - s) / ( (st - b)(t - b) ) ] * [ ( (st - b)(t - b) ) / ( (st - b)(t - b) + s k^2 ) ) ] |\n\n= | b(1 - s) / [ (st - b)(t - b) + s k^2 ) ] |.\n\nSince all terms in the denominator are negative (st - b < 0, t - b <0, s k^2 positive), but the absolute value will make it positive. So we can drop the absolute value:\n\n1/t = b(1 - s) / [ (st - b)(t - b) + s k^2 ) ]\n\nMultiply both sides by denominator:\n\n[ (st - b)(t - b) + s k^2 ) ] / t = b(1 - s)\n\nMultiply both sides by t:\n\n(st - b)(t - b) + s k^2 = b t (1 - s)\n\nExpand (st - b)(t - b):\n\n= st(t - b) - b(t - b) = st^2 - s t b - b t + b^2\n\nTherefore, left side:\n\nst^2 - s t b - b t + b^2 + s k^2\n\nRight side:\n\nb t - b t s\n\nBring all terms to left side:\n\nst^2 - s t b - b t + b^2 + s k^2 - b t + b t s = 0\n\nWait, no. Wait, the right side is b t (1 - s). So when we bring everything to left:\n\nst^2 - s t b - b t + b^2 + s k^2 - b t + b t s = 0\n\nWait, let me check again.\n\nOriginal left side after expansion: st\u00b2 - stb - bt + b\u00b2 + s k\u00b2\n\nOriginal right side: bt(1 - s) = bt - bts\n\nSo moving right side to left:\n\nst\u00b2 - stb - bt + b\u00b2 + s k\u00b2 - bt + bts = 0\n\nSimplify term by term:\n\nst\u00b2: st\u00b2\n\n-stb + bts: -stb + bts = 0\n\n-bt - bt: -2bt\n\nb\u00b2: +b\u00b2\n\ns k\u00b2: +s k\u00b2\n\nThus, left side becomes:\n\nst\u00b2 - 2bt + b\u00b2 + s k\u00b2 = 0\n\nSo the equation is:\n\nst\u00b2 - 2bt + b\u00b2 + s k\u00b2 = 0\n\nWe can factor this as:\n\ns(t\u00b2 + k\u00b2) - 2bt + b\u00b2 = 0\n\nTherefore:\n\ns(t\u00b2 + k\u00b2) = 2bt - b\u00b2\n\nThus:\n\ns = (2bt - b\u00b2)/(t\u00b2 + k\u00b2)\n\nTherefore, we have s expressed in 